# VoidBale

VoidBale is an asynchronous, token-only Python framework for building Bale Messenger bots.

## Design

VoidBale exposes only the Bale Bot API model. It does not implement user authentication, user sessions, MTProto, phone login, QR login, account clients, or self-bot functionality.

## Minimal bot

```python
from voidbale import Bot

bot = Bot("YOUR_BALE_BOT_TOKEN")

@bot.command("start")
async def start(message):
    await message.answer("Hello from VoidBale")

bot.run()
```

## Webhook

```python
from voidbale import Bot
from voidbale.webhook import WebhookServer

bot = Bot("YOUR_BALE_BOT_TOKEN")

@bot.command("start")
async def start(message):
    await message.answer("Webhook is working")

bot.run_webhook("https://example.com/bale/webhook", host="0.0.0.0", port=8080, path="/bale/webhook")
```

## Filters

```python
from voidbale import Bot, F

bot = Bot("YOUR_BALE_BOT_TOKEN")

@bot.message(F.text == "ping")
async def ping(message):
    await message.answer("pong")

@bot.message(F.command("help"))
async def help_command(message):
    await message.answer("help")
```

## Keyboards

```python
from voidbale import Bot, InlineKeyboard

bot = Bot("YOUR_BALE_BOT_TOKEN")

keyboard = InlineKeyboard().button("Open", url="https://bale.ai").button("Ping", callback_data="ping").adjust(2)

@bot.command("start")
async def start(message):
    await message.answer("Choose", reply_markup=keyboard)

@bot.callback_query(F.data == "ping")
async def callback(query):
    await query.answer("pong")
```

## API

The `Bot` object provides direct async wrappers for the common Bale Bot API operations and `bot.request()` for any Bot API method exposed by the configured Bale endpoint.

The library accepts only a bot token and communicates through the Bale Bot API. No user-account client is included.
